            "96": "3) Green, Yellow, Black\nThe Olympic flag was designed by Pierre de Coubertin, the founder of the modern Olympic Games. The five rings represent the five inhabited continents. The colors were chosen to represent the nations participating in the games. The colors are blue, yellow, black, green, and red. The rings are green, yellow, black, which corresponds to the colors of the continents represented.",
