            "96": "3) Green, Yellow, Black\nThe five rings on the Olympic flag are designed to represent the continents. The top row, from left to right, features Green (representing Europe), Yellow (representing Asia), and Black (representing Africa).",
            "97": "4) Basketball\nA slam dunk is a basketball-specific move involving forcefully throwing the ball downwards through the hoop. It is not performed in volleyball, handball, or tennis.",
            "98": "1) Arthur Conan Doyle\nArthur Conan Doyle is the author responsible for creating the iconic detective Sherlock Holmes and his stories.",
            "99": "3) 15\nA strike is worth 10 pins, and a spare is worth 10 pins. If you throw a strike and then another strike, the score is 10 + 10 = 20. However, the question specifies \"without striking twice or throwing a spare,\" meaning you can only get a maximum of 15 points in a single frame if you knock down all 10 pins on your first ball.",
